@@@@ REPLACE
and the statuses 408, 429, 500, 502, 503 and 504. Every other failure ends the request at once.
`max_delay` bounds the computed backoff only; a `Retry-After` is bounded by `max_wait` and the
request `deadline`. Invalid values are rejected when the configuration loads. As in every section, an
unknown key is a warning, not an error (ADR-004), so a misspelt key such as `max_attemps` leaves the
default in force: run `courier config check` after editing to see such warnings.

## [rate_limit]
